# [deps]-based cross-project monomorphization: extends `cross_project_dep` (plain
# cross-project `use`, no monomorphization) the same way `monomorphize_cross_file_main.br`
# extends `cross_file_use_main.br` (plain same-project cross-file `use`) -- adds a
# turbofish-triggered generic specialization on top.
#
# `Wrapper<T>` (with a `type let T` field depending on its own type parameter -- see
# tests/cases/fixtures/dep_monomorphize/src/wrapper.br's own doc comment and
# src/transpiler/monomorphize.rs's module doc comment) is declared in the DEPENDENCY
# project, resolved via this project's own `boring.toml` `[deps] wrapperlib =
# "../fixtures/dep_monomorphize"`. The concrete turbofish construction site
# (`Wrapper<string>(...)`) lives HERE, in the CONSUMING project -- a different file,
# and a different `[deps]` project, than the one declaring `Wrapper<T>`. The
# transpiler specializes a non-generic `Wrapper_string` clone into the DECLARING
# file's own emitted module and rewrites this call site to a plain call on that
# specialized name, proving monomorphization's whole-reachable-file-graph collection
# extends across a `[deps]` project boundary, not just a same-project `use`.
#
# Registered as `interp_test!`-style `#[test] fn cross_project_dep_monomorphize`
# (tests/run.rs, `boring run` against this same src/main.br),
# `transpile_project_test!(cross_project_dep_monomorphize)` (tests/transpile.rs,
# project-mode `boring build` + a real `cargo run`), and
# `emit_rust_includes_deps_cross_project_monomorphized_module` (tests/emit_rust_modules.rs,
# `--emit-rust` + real `rustc`).
use wrapperlib.wrapper.*

let w = Wrapper<string>("hi")
print w.value
print w.get()
